@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- WHICH TAX YEARS THIS TEXT ANSWERS.
--
-- The deposited source is one text: s 66 as consolidated at retrieval on
-- 2026-10-06.  Its amendment list (line 2454) ends
--     "... תשע״ח־5, תשפ״ב־5, תשפ״ג־2, תשפ״ג־6, תשפ״ד־3"
-- and the page header (line 5) resolves the last two to
--     ס״ח תשפ״ג, 400  "חוק הגדלת נקודות זיכוי להורים במס הכנסה והרחבת מענק עבודה"
--     ס״ח תשפ״ד, 630  "חוק סיוע להורים לילדים עד גיל שלוש (תיקוני חקיקה)"
-- (the code תשפ״ד־3 is the third 5784 entry; תשפ״ג־6 the sixth 5783 entry,
-- counting pages 163, 171 and 177 as three entries).
--
-- Both amended s 66(c)(4)-(5).  Two Israel Tax Authority circulars, an aid and
-- not a source of law, say when (full citations, sha256 and retrieval in
-- NOTES.md section 7):
--   * 2024-000012 of 3 January 2024: the 5783 law, published in Sefer
--     HaChukim 3048, amended ss 40 and 66 "החל משנת המס 2024";
--   * 2024-001090 of 26 March 2024: the 5784 law, published 20.03.2024 in
--     Sefer HaChukim 3184, amended ss 40 and 66 "החל משנת המס 2024", and
--     "חוק זה יחול רטרואקטיבית החל מיום 1.1.2024".
-- The amending Acts themselves could not be fetched (fs.knesset.gov.il
-- answered with a geographic block), so the commencement is taken from the
-- circulars and recorded as assumption A1.
--
-- So the deposited text is the s 66 that governs tax years from 2024.  For an
-- earlier tax year the children's credit points certainly differed (the 2024
-- circulars print the 2023 figures) and other paragraphs may have; this
-- encoding does not hold that text, and REFUSES rather than answering an
-- earlier year with the later law.  For a tax year after 2026 the answer is a
-- projection of the text as it stood on 2026-10-06 (assumption A2).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66 — the tax years this text answers`

@ref ITA circulars 2024-000012 (3.1.2024) and 2024-001090 (26.3.2024): the amendments תשפ״ג־6 and תשפ״ד־3 to s 66 apply from tax year 2024
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year the deposited text of section 66 governs` MEANS 2024

@ref s 66 amendment list, line 2454; the text before the תשפ״ג־6 and תשפ״ד־3 amendments is not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"

-- Every top-level rule of the row asks this first: the answer it computes
-- stands for a tax year the deposited text governs, and is refused otherwise.
GIVEN a          IS A TYPE
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `answer`   IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`in tax year` `the year` `, the answer is` `answer` MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST `the first tax year the deposited text of section 66 governs`
    THEN `answer`
    ELSE `this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024`

§§ `Tax years -- illustrations`

#ASSERT `in tax year` 2024 `, the answer is` 7 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `in tax year` 2026 `, the answer is` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `in tax year` 2023 `, the answer is` 7
        BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"
